---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Learn about Jiangge Wu — a senior backend engineer based in Singapore with 9+ years of backend engineering experience, including roles at TikTok and Shopee."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <SectionHeading title="About Me" />

    <div class="space-y-6 text-surface-700 leading-relaxed dark:text-surface-300">
      <p>
        I'm a senior backend engineer based in Singapore with over 9 years of experience building
        large-scale distributed systems and backend infrastructure using Go and Java.
      </p>

      <p>
        I specialize in scalable storage platforms, distributed services, caching systems,
        resiliency engineering, and backend platform reliability. I've spent my career operating
        mission-critical systems serving high-scale international products at companies like
        TikTok and Shopee.
      </p>

      <p>
        Beyond my day job, I also work with Swift and SwiftUI to build iOS applications,
        and I've integrated AI APIs into products to deliver intelligent features to end users.
        I enjoy the process of turning ideas into functional, well-structured software &mdash;
        whether it's a globally distributed storage platform or a mobile app solving a personal need.
      </p>

      <p>
        I hold a Master of Science in Information Systems from Nanyang Technological University
        and a Bachelor of Engineering in Software Engineering from Tianjin University.
      </p>

      <h3 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">How I Work</h3>

      <p>
        I believe in keeping things simple until complexity is justified. I prefer clear documentation
        over tribal knowledge, automated tests over manual verification, and incremental delivery over
        big-bang releases. I value collaboration and direct communication, and I try to approach
        every problem with curiosity and pragmatism.
      </p>

      <h3 class="pt-4 text-lg font-semibold text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Technical Focus</h3>

      <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-surface-200 p-4 dark:border-surface-700">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Backend Engineering</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400">
            Go, Java, Python, REST APIs, microservices, system design
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-surface-200 p-4 dark:border-surface-700">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Distributed Systems</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400">
            Service reliability, fault tolerance, scalability engineering
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-surface-200 p-4 dark:border-surface-700">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Data & Storage</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400">
            MySQL, Redis, Memcached, Kafka, Cassandra, object storage
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-surface-200 p-4 dark:border-surface-700">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">Infrastructure & Mobile</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400">
            Docker, cloud infrastructure, Swift, SwiftUI, iOS development
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="rounded-lg border border-surface-200 p-4 dark:border-surface-700 sm:col-span-2">
          <h4 class="font-medium text-surface-900 dark:text-surface-100">AI-Native Engineering</h4>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-surface-600 dark:text-surface-400">
            Agent orchestration, tool calling, RAG pipelines, embedding search, prompt engineering, LLM API integration
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
